this is a bit of raised ground to the  east of harkeve where the russians try  to use a tree line to give their one of  their armored columns some protection  and cover  in vain as it turns out because along  the stretch of land there is just one  wrecked russian tank or piece of heavy  armor after another but before that  happened the ukrainians say the russians  used these positions to carry out war  crimes they shelled the villages below  and they also shelled civilian vehicles  trying to bring aid to  the villages so we've been out this  morning filming ukrainian and lithuanian  investigators combing this land going  through the foxholes and camps and the  and the wrecked armor looking for any  evidence looking for names of soldiers  looking for documents anything that  links these soldiers with what they say  were war crimes and then they're going  to link that with what they found in the  villages below so early this week we  filmed a body being exumed he was a man  who had been out feeding his animals  when the russians shelled his home  killing him outright and his poor wife  had to bury him on her own so he's been  exhumed as part of this investigation  because  the facts of the rules of war mean that  anyone who is found guilty of attacking  civilians deliberately without any  military justification  is guilty of a war crime and this is  part of a much broader investigation  across all the land the ukrainians are  reclaiming from the russians  trying to prove that the invaders  carried out atrocities and the  investigator we spoke to says he's  confident  that the russians who they are building  evidence against here will eventually be  brought to justice
 

